  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "break, continue and nested loops"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "break leaves the innermost loop at once; continue skips the rest of the current iteration and goes to the next test (in a for loop, after the update). In nested loops the inner loop runs completely for every iteration of the outer loop, so an outer loop of 4 and an inner loop of 3 run the inner body 12 times. Patterns of stars and numbers are printed with nested loops: the outer loop counts rows, the inner loop counts columns."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "break: leave the loop"
    },
    {
     "en": "continue: skip to the next iteration"
    },
    {
     "en": "Nested: inner runs fully for each outer pass"
    },
    {
     "en": "Patterns: outer = rows, inner = columns"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "break leaves the innermost loop at once; continue skips the rest of the current iteration and goes to the next test (in a for loop, after the update). In nested loops the inner loop runs completely for every iteration of the outer loop, so an outer loop of 4 and an inner loop of 3 run the inner body 12 times. Patterns of stars and numbers are printed with nested loops: the outer loop counts rows, the inner loop counts columns."
   }
